You freeze on the spot, trying hastily to come up with something, but your body refuses to obey; you can't even think. Suddenly, Conan springs to the fire with a war cry, snatches out a flaming firebrand, and hurls it at the chest of the dreadful beast. It recoils with a wild howl filling the forest. Conan keeps throwing burning branches at the beast, shouting as loud as he can.

The beast retreats. It is an old, experienced predator that knows how painfully the fire can bite. Moving backwards, it roars with fright and anger once again, and then in the twinkling of an eye, the creature disappears into the thicket. Conan collapses to the ground.